    {
      "id": "clm:522b4a4e9c98c77175a5a6747e5ef36653656ab504f5fa43ee20e049f404ceb6",
      "text": "When history traversal raises incomplete-history, the donor compares the current rollback identifier with the identifier captured at construction and aborts if it changed. If it has not changed, retryable-write records and prepared or committed transaction records produce a lost-history sentinel; other transaction states are skipped, and the iterator is reset. The rollback fixture increments the rollback identifier and asserts that the next history fetch throws. The incomplete-history fixture asserts a sentinel with the incomplete-history statement identifier, followed by exhaustion. These are fixture assertions, not integration or workload measurements. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source.cpp",
      "also": [
