    {
      "id": "clm:d525974324b27139203b68e077555c4df095adb583d76465cad7eb89f2f2a054",
      "text": "Treat this evidence as the historical MongoDB 7.0.22 source-defined session-history protocol. The donor explicitly substitutes lost-history markers because it does not support retrying entire transactions; the recipient records retryable history as no-ops without setting the persisted transaction-state field. These mechanisms do not establish full transaction replay. Do not extrapolate them into a universal client retry guarantee, measured latency, replication-lag throttling, current-release behavior, CDC sink co-commit or a production-safety guarantee. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source.cpp",
      "also": [
