    {
      "id": "clm:cf59691cb5aeea7b0fa228350e47c8d27df7ae15273dbb8d28ac0ae8263ce408",
      "text": "When a session-history source exists, the cloner forwards non-null retryable-write operation times into its history queue. The transaction-commit handler excludes non-retryable internal sessions and queues each eligible touched namespace with an active cloner at most once. The donor fixture for writes arriving after depletion repeatedly asserts that newly queued entries become fetchable and require a majority wait. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/migration_chunk_cloner_source.cpp",
      "also": [
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source_test.cpp",
