    {
      "id": "clm:65aadbcaa3605095d8c17c1f3843b6aecbdf688216cf297dc5d0899f05d48999",
      "text": "The donor looks up a retry image by session identity and can forge an image no-op only when the image exists and its transaction number matches the originating operation. It copies the image, session and statement information, and emits the image before its operation. Both receive parent-session identity conversion when necessary. If no usable image exists, it strips needsRetryImage; the source comment says a destination retry then surfaces an error, so the transfer does not promise successful retry-result reconstruction for an unavailable image. Classic image links instead fetch the referenced oplog record. The recipient rewrites the image reference to a local oplog image link. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source.cpp",
      "also": [
