    {
      "id": "clm:77c1c0821af5f05d37f4a65a910e16270ac74b59d11a2f3c7d4be7c10e81f646",
      "text": "The donor batch builder chooses the highest operation time among entries marked as requiring a majority wait. The command handler waits for that operation time, then checks the rollback identifier; its comment requires this ordering so a rolled-back entry cannot escape detection. The header separately specifies that callers must reject a change of term within a batch. The cited implementation shows the majority wait and rollback check; it does not justify attributing an explicit term-comparison branch to the batch-building loop. The session-mods command waits on a notification when it has no batch and continues until it has entries or completion; returned batches participate in that stateful buffer-draining protocol. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/migration_chunk_cloner_source.cpp",
      "also": [
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/migration_chunk_cloner_source_legacy_commands.cpp",
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source.h",
