    {
      "id": "clm:c32b787330807e4ac272e8d097bbdb11a411819a0cf4ab49b28443e846cba2e1",
      "text": "start changes NotStarted to Migrating and spawns the transfer thread. On an empty batch, the recipient majority-waits for its last local result and changes Migrating to ReadyToCommit only if it is still Migrating after that wait. This first-drain state is not Done. finish changes a non-error state to Committing. Readiness leaves the retrieval loop active for the finish signal and additional donor history. The public class interface distinguishes migrating, ready-to-commit, committing, error and done states. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_destination.cpp",
      "also": [
