    {
      "id": "clm:4f09fe81ced522bbc0c480d240ca7651e0bf016bc279a4edbe2523e619b47155",
      "text": "Calling finish changes the recipient state to committing unless an error is already recorded. In the retrieval loop, the first empty batch observed in committing sets the post-commit drain flag and performs a majority wait; a later empty batch observed in committing breaks the loop. The flag is not reset on a nonempty batch. After the loop, the worker again waits for majority acknowledgement of its last local history operation before setting done. The fixture success helper supplies two empty responses after finish and asserts done after joining. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_destination.cpp",
      "also": [
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_destination_test.cpp",
