    {
      "id": "clm:c2c0121dbe2023be4367eaf3be57ceef50ceb3c087ac54548fcd354c7c2e6a0e",
      "text": "Cancelable operation contexts cover recipient fetches, entry processing and the final majority wait; they are marked interruptible on stepdown or stepup. The worker records most DBExceptions as ErrorOccurred, and forceFail records that state too. The legacy CommandNotFound exception returns from the worker without setting Done. join waits for the spawned thread; the destructor records an error and joins if necessary. Manager failure paths force the session worker into an error state. The network-error fixture asserts that joining completes with an error state and a nonempty message. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_destination.cpp",
      "also": [
