    {
      "id": "clm:047066ab51196f7622ee9c2d1419cde68d00f0f589a125bcf21c816b69dc0877",
      "text": "Committed retryable internal transactions are traversed as history: commit-transaction entries are skipped, and apply-operations entries are unrolled. Inner operations must have statement identifiers and the migrating namespace, then pass the shared filter. CRUD entries require a chunk key in range. Rewritten migration-tagged no-ops also undergo that range check unless they are incomplete-history markers; other no-ops pass without a chunk-key check. The committed-internal-transaction fixture includes an owning-shard-change no-op among the expected transferred operations. Before transfer, internal retryable-session identities and transaction numbers are rewritten to the parent retryable-write identity and parent transaction number. This is conversion of retryable history rather than transaction execution. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source.cpp",
      "also": [
        "https://api.github.com/repos/mongodb/mongo/git/ref/tags/r7.0.22",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/mongodb/mongo/git/tags/ef98696d6009abf1b6f73a935c9f7bb3fa3ea4c4",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v7.0/release-notes/7.0/",
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source_test.cpp"
      ],
