    {
      "id": "clm:53a6b041d9792b84e47be2cf79d65f04f31ca4b67a8f6d6dff5e7a8a22173b53",
      "text": "Initial history is fetched before queued writes. Initial-history records and image no-ops return shouldWaitForMajority false; new originating writes return true. Cleanup signals terminal completion. Otherwise pending writes take precedence over commit-started state, so buffered history must still drain after commit starts. Commit-start and cleanup wake waiting consumers. Newly queued operation times wake a waiting notification to request another fetch. Temporary depletion therefore differs from terminal drain. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source.h",
      "also": [
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_source.cpp",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/mongodb/mongo/git/ref/tags/r7.0.22",
