    {
      "id": "clm:2ca18d0c2484507a58110afed295c5d8fbad45253648bb44c1d45aa4501c681b",
      "text": "For history entries it replays, the recipient reconstructs image links using the preceding locally inserted image operation time and requires matching session and transaction identities. It converts retry-image markers to the classic pre-image or post-image link and clears the marker. It rejects a second image while the previous local result is an image, an unexpected classic image link without a preceding image, or a replayed operation following an image without the required link. The forged-pre-image fixture asserts that the outer migrated record has a pre-image link, has no retry-image marker, and points to an image with the original object. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_destination.cpp",
      "also": [
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/dacdbc3df2fbe579b03336a2f01fc9aedf406a41/src/mongo/db/s/session_catalog_migration_destination_test.cpp",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/mongodb/mongo/git/ref/tags/r7.0.22",
